% decline_eq_bad.glp — FR-036 DECLINE (NEGATIVE: must be REJECTED at load).
% == (Prolog term identity) is NOT a GLP guard: it is a redundant alias of =?=
% over ground terms (Tier-3 ISO/Prolog idiom, deliberately absent from the GLP
% kernel). A clause using it in guard position must be rejected. This file is
% identical in shape to order_guards.glp's lt/1 except the declined guard, so the
% rejection isolates the decline. Canonical GLP form: X? =?= Y?.
exported procedure deq(_?, _?, _).
deq(X, Y, yes) :- X? == Y? | true.
